      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test creates a `PercentCodec` configured to always encode null bytes (all-zero array), encodes a 5-null-byte array, then decodes it back. I'll improve it with meaningful variable names and explanatory comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated names (`byteArray0`, `object0`, `object1`, `percentCodec0`) with descriptive ones (`nullBytes`, `encodedResult`, `decodedResult`, `percentCodec`) and adds inline comments that explain the codec configuration, the encoding behavior (null bytes → `%00`), and the intent of each assertion."
